<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1588" root="ايد" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْيِدٌ</span></b> , of the same measure as <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْمِنٌ</span>, <i>A great,
mighty,</i> or <i>severe, thing;</i> (S, L, K;) <i>a calamity:</i>
(T, S, M, L, K:) or, accord. to As, it is ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْيَدٌ</span></b> ,
with fet-h to the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ى</span>, and signifies <i>anything rendered strong,</i> or <i>hard,</i> or <i>severe.</i> (L.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآوِدُ</span>,
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اود</span>.)

